    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "If $z_{min}$ and $z_{max}$ are the upper and lower bounds to $z$, then $p(z) = 0$ outside of this range, and over the entire range $\\int_{z_{min}}^{z_{max}} p(z) dz = 1$. Both of these properties are in accord with common sense — a probability is never negative, and the total probability of all possible outcomes is one. A large number of functions fulfill these properties, and they have been studied in considerable detail (Johnson and Kotz 1970a,b, 1972; Kendall and Stuart 1977).",
