    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The most useful probability density functions are defined completely by one or two parameters describing the central location and dispersion of the distribution. The most widely used measure of the location is the arithmetic mean, $ \\mu $, also known as the first moment about the origin. If $ p(z) $ is the probability density function of phenotype z, then weighting all values of z by their density leads to",
