      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ E(z) $ denotes the expected value or expectation of z. Here, we have arbitrarily put the limits $ \\pm\\infty $ on the integral to ensure that the entire range of variation is covered. For discrete characters, $ \\mu = E(z) = \\sum_{i} z_{i}P(z = z_{i}) $. For a character denoted by z, the sample estimate of the mean is generally denoted by $ \\bar{z} $, and estimated as the average of the n measures,",
